From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
Date: 2026-07-29
Subject: [PATCH 09] fix: serialise make_prepped_xfer to prevent NIXL_ERR_INVALID_PARAM

NixlStorageAgent holds two shared pre-built NIXL dlist handles built at
init time: mem_xfer_handler (registered L1 DRAM buffer) and
storage_xfer_handler (registered NVMe slot file pool).

Both get_mem_to_storage_handle() and get_storage_to_mem_handle() call
nixl_agent.make_prepped_xfer() with these shared handles and caller-
supplied index subsets.  When --max-gpu-workers > 1 or
--l2-prefetch-max-in-flight > 1, multiple asyncio coroutines interleave
at every 'await' in post_non_blocking and reach make_prepped_xfer()
concurrently.  The NIXL C++ makeXferReq() is not thread-safe for
concurrent calls on the same shared dlist handle, raising:

  nixl_rocm._bindings.nixlInvalidParamError: NIXL_ERR_INVALID_PARAM

This silently zeros all L2 reads (agent_rx_bytes_total stays 0,
ext_hit stays 0%) even when KV chunks are on NVMe, and causes request
timeouts as prefetch tasks fail and queue up.

Observed: SPUR MI355X gfx950, NIXL POSIX backend, LMCache v0.5.2,
c=32 per-client prefix with max-gpu-workers=4.

Fix: add _xfer_handle_lock (threading.Lock) in __init__ and hold it in
both handle-creation helpers. Lock scope covers only makeXferReq(), not
the subsequent async DMA transfer, so in-flight transfers stay parallel.

Applies after patches 01-08.
---
--- a/lmcache/v1/distributed/l2_adapters/nixl_store_l2_adapter.py
+++ b/lmcache/v1/distributed/l2_adapters/nixl_store_l2_adapter.py
@@ -237,6 +237,12 @@
         else:
             raise TypeError(f"Unsupported backend type: {self.backend}")
 
+        # Lock serialising calls to make_prepped_xfer().
+        # The NIXL C++ makeXferReq() is not safe to call concurrently on the
+        # same pre-built dlist handles (mem_xfer_handler / storage_xfer_handler).
+        # Concurrent calls produce nixlInvalidParamError: NIXL_ERR_INVALID_PARAM.
+        self._xfer_handle_lock = threading.Lock()
+
     def init_mem_handlers(self, device, buffer_ptr, buffer_size, page_size, device_id):
         """
         Initialize memory handlers for the given device and buffer.
@@ -363,23 +369,27 @@
     def get_mem_to_storage_handle(self, mem_indices, storage_indices) -> NixlXferHandle:
         """Get a Nixl transfer handle for transferring data from memory to storage."""
 
-        return self.nixl_agent.make_prepped_xfer(
-            "WRITE",
-            self.mem_xfer_handler,
-            mem_indices,
-            self.storage_xfer_handler,
-            storage_indices,
-        )
+        # Serialise: makeXferReq is not thread-safe on shared dlist handles.
+        with self._xfer_handle_lock:
+            return self.nixl_agent.make_prepped_xfer(
+                "WRITE",
+                self.mem_xfer_handler,
+                mem_indices,
+                self.storage_xfer_handler,
+                storage_indices,
+            )
 
     def get_storage_to_mem_handle(self, mem_indices, storage_indices) -> NixlXferHandle:
         """Get a Nixl transfer handle for transferring data from storage to memory."""
-        return self.nixl_agent.make_prepped_xfer(
-            "READ",
-            self.mem_xfer_handler,
-            mem_indices,
-            self.storage_xfer_handler,
-            storage_indices,
-        )
+        # Serialise: makeXferReq is not thread-safe on shared dlist handles.
+        with self._xfer_handle_lock:
+            return self.nixl_agent.make_prepped_xfer(
+                "READ",
+                self.mem_xfer_handler,
+                mem_indices,
+                self.storage_xfer_handler,
+                storage_indices,
+            )
 
     def post_blocking(self, handle: NixlXferHandle):
         """Post a Nixl transfer handle and block until the transfer is done."""
